# XBD <nl_types.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Value relations of <nl_types.h>: NL_CAT_LOCALE differs from the 0 that
# catopen() reads as a different request, and NL_SETD and nl_catd are
# usable as catgets() and catopen() use them. Each says why it has no
# mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.nl_types.h.001
anchor     basedefs/nl_types.h.html#DESCRIPTION/NL_CAT_LOCALE
anchor     functions/catopen.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       NL_CAT_LOCALE is a value that can be passed as the int oflag argument
           of catopen() and it is not 0.
note       Not stated for the header: catopen() treats 0 and NL_CAT_LOCALE as two
           different requests (LANG, or the LC_MESSAGES locale category), so the
           values have to differ (Q-169).
test       t/001-cat-locale.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.nl_types.h.002
anchor     basedefs/nl_types.h.html#DESCRIPTION/NL_SETD
anchor     functions/catopen.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       NL_SETD has a value that can be passed as the int set_id argument of
           catgets(), and (nl_catd)-1, the error return of catopen(), is a valid
           nl_catd value that compares equal to itself.
note       The value of NL_SETD is implementation-defined, so only its use as an
           int is checked.
test       t/002-setd-catd.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
